1
00:00:08,870 --> 00:00:11,705
The palualo ritual of
the Ilokano people stems

2
00:00:11,706 --> 00:00:14,666
from their pre-Christian animistic beliefs,

3
00:00:14,667 --> 00:00:18,170
where ancestral and nature spirits
were central to life.

4
00:00:18,171 --> 00:00:19,588
Similar to the atang,

5
00:00:19,589 --> 00:00:24,051
it appeases spirits to ensure
harmony, health, and prosperity.

6
00:00:24,052 --> 00:00:26,094
Even with the spread of Christianity,

7
00:00:26,095 --> 00:00:27,763
these practices persist,

8
00:00:27,764 --> 00:00:30,348
blending Catholic elements with tradition.

9
00:00:30,349 --> 00:00:33,894
Calling out names of departed
loved ones during a palualo

10
00:00:33,895 --> 00:00:37,439
ties ancestral remembrance
to preventing misfortune,

11
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:40,443
curing illnesses, and expressing gratitude.

12
00:00:48,326 --> 00:00:52,329
It reflects the Ilokano view of the
interconnected realms of the living,

13
00:00:52,330 --> 00:00:53,122
the dead,

14
00:00:53,122 --> 00:00:53,915
and the spiritual,

15
00:00:53,916 --> 00:00:58,795
uniting families, preserving traditions,
and affirming their identity.

16
00:01:10,973 --> 00:01:11,973
Ugly!

17
00:01:14,435 --> 00:01:15,520
Ugly!

18
00:01:17,897 --> 00:01:19,314
Hey, ugly!

19
00:01:19,315 --> 00:01:20,690
Let me enter.

20
00:01:20,691 --> 00:01:23,276
I swear to God, if I see you naked...

21
00:01:23,277 --> 00:01:24,736
I'm telling you.

22
00:01:24,737 --> 00:01:26,489
I will hit you.

23
00:01:27,949 --> 00:01:29,450
Ugly!

24
00:01:31,911 --> 00:01:34,162
Did I tell you to come in?

25
00:01:34,163 --> 00:01:36,039
Your dad is looking for you.

26
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:38,042
What happened to you?

27
00:01:41,254 --> 00:01:43,714
I just have a lot on my mind.

28
00:01:45,967 --> 00:01:47,926
You know, Jorge...

29
00:01:47,927 --> 00:01:50,011
We're still young.

30
00:01:50,012 --> 00:01:52,055
We still have a lot of time.

31
00:01:52,056 --> 00:01:55,308
That's why... let's not
think of ourselves for now.

32
00:01:55,309 --> 00:01:58,812
Our duty now is to be
present for the adults.

33
00:01:58,813 --> 00:02:03,775
For them, they have a
shorter time left to grieve.

34
00:02:03,776 --> 00:02:04,735
That's why, come on.

35
00:02:04,736 --> 00:02:06,404
Get up.

36
00:02:06,737 --> 00:02:08,739
What are you talking about?

37
00:02:10,283 --> 00:02:11,283
Come on.

38
00:02:11,284 --> 00:02:12,909
Spill the tea.

39
00:02:12,910 --> 00:02:15,288
What happened between you and Kiko?

40
00:02:25,089 --> 00:02:26,882
Kiko's leaving me.

41
00:02:26,883 --> 00:02:28,008
What?

42
00:02:28,009 --> 00:02:29,092
That was fast.

43
00:02:29,093 --> 00:02:30,927
You're not even official yet.

44
00:02:30,928 --> 00:02:32,762
He's going to Manila.

45
00:02:32,763 --> 00:02:34,557
He's going to study there.

46
00:02:35,057 --> 00:02:37,058
My God, Jorge.

47
00:02:37,059 --> 00:02:39,437
I know, I know.

48
00:02:40,104 --> 00:02:43,106
The first one to fall, loses.

49
00:02:43,107 --> 00:02:44,858
Forget that.

50
00:02:44,859 --> 00:02:47,694
Why are you listening to a fool like me?

51
00:02:47,695 --> 00:02:49,446
Isn't that what you're gonna say?

52
00:02:49,447 --> 00:02:50,822
No.

53
00:02:50,823 --> 00:02:52,741
I was going to say...

54
00:02:52,742 --> 00:02:55,619
It's better to have loved and lost...

55
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:57,538
That's it.

56
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:04,045
Why would I listen to you?

57
00:03:05,087 --> 00:03:06,379
When...

58
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:08,966
You’re a fool.

59
00:03:09,717 --> 00:03:11,843
See, you're not the fool.

60
00:03:11,844 --> 00:03:13,304
I am.

61
00:03:13,888 --> 00:03:15,681
Good thing you know.

62
00:03:16,974 --> 00:03:19,267
Do you think you're the main character?

63
00:03:19,268 --> 00:03:21,770
I also have my life.

64
00:03:21,771 --> 00:03:23,480
Remember Cutie?

65
00:03:23,481 --> 00:03:25,107
They confessed.

66
00:03:25,608 --> 00:03:29,444
It's why I have a different
perspective on love now.

67
00:03:29,445 --> 00:03:30,446
Sweet.

68
00:03:30,905 --> 00:03:32,073
Amazing.

69
00:03:32,365 --> 00:03:33,866
- And...
- Fine.

70
00:03:35,076 --> 00:03:36,368
Well, excuse me.

71
00:03:36,369 --> 00:03:38,328
I'm only a supporting character.

72
00:03:38,329 --> 00:03:40,830
Yes, supporting character.

73
00:03:40,831 --> 00:03:42,375
That's why, Jorge.

74
00:03:43,084 --> 00:03:46,045
You need to fight for who you love.

75
00:03:46,879 --> 00:03:48,546
What did you say?

76
00:03:48,547 --> 00:03:49,965
You need to...

77
00:03:49,966 --> 00:03:51,467
Fight for who you love.

78
00:03:52,635 --> 00:03:53,677
You already know.

79
00:03:53,678 --> 00:03:56,763
Why do you have to make me repeat it?

80
00:03:56,764 --> 00:03:57,473
Ruth.

81
00:03:57,474 --> 00:03:59,141
That was the problem with Grandpa.

82
00:03:59,934 --> 00:04:01,227
He didn't fight for it.

83
00:04:02,436 --> 00:04:03,728
Grandpa?

84
00:04:03,729 --> 00:04:04,981
Huh?

85
00:04:06,482 --> 00:04:08,275
Obscenity!

86
00:04:08,276 --> 00:04:10,318
Oh, you're wearing shorts.

87
00:04:10,319 --> 00:04:12,696
Of course, it was hard back then.

88
00:04:12,697 --> 00:04:14,948
It was a different time then.

89
00:04:14,949 --> 00:04:16,157
There were lots of evil people.

90
00:04:16,158 --> 00:04:17,492
Close-minded.

91
00:04:17,493 --> 00:04:18,910
But even then...

92
00:04:18,911 --> 00:04:21,121
You have to be brave.

93
00:04:21,122 --> 00:04:22,581
Huh?

94
00:04:23,916 --> 00:04:25,792
We have to take charge.

95
00:04:25,793 --> 00:04:27,002
What are you saying?

96
00:04:27,003 --> 00:04:28,003
Ruth.

97
00:04:28,004 --> 00:04:29,421
Thank you.

98
00:04:29,422 --> 00:04:32,008
I’m going to Kiko.

99
00:04:34,302 --> 00:04:35,845
I'm going.

100
00:04:37,096 --> 00:04:38,597
Oh.

101
00:04:38,598 --> 00:04:41,392
People in love are crazy.

102
00:04:44,061 --> 00:04:45,903
It's a good thing you were able to visit.

103
00:04:45,928 --> 00:04:50,529
Yes. Our car even broke down. We travelled
so far and we got stuck in traffic.

104
00:04:53,237 --> 00:04:54,654
Jorge.

105
00:04:54,655 --> 00:04:56,031
Later, Dad.

106
00:04:56,032 --> 00:04:57,574
I'm in a hurry.

107
00:04:57,575 --> 00:04:58,826
Jorge.

108
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:00,369
Was that your son?

109
00:05:08,627 --> 00:05:10,129
He's my son.

110
00:05:17,511 --> 00:05:19,180
Jorge!

111
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:32,500
"All the Things I Leave You"
(Episode 6)

112
00:05:34,820 --> 00:05:36,613
Kiko?

113
00:05:36,614 --> 00:05:37,906
Is anyone here?

114
00:05:37,907 --> 00:05:39,492
Kiko?

115
00:05:39,867 --> 00:05:42,118
Kiko, come out.

116
00:05:42,119 --> 00:05:43,996
Kiko!

117
00:05:46,415 --> 00:05:47,917
Jasmine.

118
00:05:48,542 --> 00:05:49,918
Do you still remember me?

119
00:05:49,919 --> 00:05:52,546
Manong Kiko's boyfriend?

120
00:05:54,090 --> 00:05:55,508
Yes.

121
00:05:56,008 --> 00:05:57,425
Where is he?

122
00:05:57,426 --> 00:05:58,885
He went out.

123
00:05:58,886 --> 00:06:00,553
Where did he go?

124
00:06:00,554 --> 00:06:02,306
To the moon.

125
00:06:02,890 --> 00:06:03,557
Moon?

126
00:06:03,558 --> 00:06:09,480
Jasmine meant...
Mun... Municipal hall.

127
00:06:11,107 --> 00:06:13,108
Oh, at the municipal hall.

128
00:06:13,109 --> 00:06:15,819
He had to attend to something there.

129
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:17,947
Color ship.

130
00:06:20,282 --> 00:06:22,450
Oh, scholarship.

131
00:06:22,451 --> 00:06:23,618
Okay.

132
00:06:23,619 --> 00:06:25,955
I'll go find your cousin.

133
00:06:26,789 --> 00:06:27,914
Thank you.

134
00:06:27,915 --> 00:06:29,917
You're welcome.

135
00:06:31,001 --> 00:06:32,837
I'll go now.

136
00:06:42,054 --> 00:06:43,054
Manong!

137
00:06:43,973 --> 00:06:44,598
Oops!

138
00:06:44,599 --> 00:06:46,474
Gotcha!

139
00:06:46,475 --> 00:06:47,935
Sorry, Nate.

140
00:06:48,227 --> 00:06:50,271
I'm in a hurry.

141
00:06:50,646 --> 00:06:51,397
I noticed.

142
00:06:51,398 --> 00:06:52,897
You kept passing by earlier.

143
00:06:52,898 --> 00:06:54,900
You weren't even hearing me.

144
00:06:55,317 --> 00:06:57,277
I will go to Kiko and...

145
00:06:57,278 --> 00:06:58,654
I need to go.

146
00:06:59,864 --> 00:07:01,114
I noticed.

147
00:07:01,115 --> 00:07:02,575
You're always with him.

148
00:07:03,117 --> 00:07:04,243
Jorge.

149
00:07:04,785 --> 00:07:07,954
I know you always got a lot
on your mind these days.

150
00:07:07,955 --> 00:07:09,915
Because your grandfather passed.

151
00:07:09,969 --> 00:07:11,344
If you need someone to talk to,

152
00:07:11,368 --> 00:07:13,204
I'm always here, you know.

153
00:07:19,884 --> 00:07:21,634
Nathan, come on!

154
00:07:21,635 --> 00:07:23,428
Get him over here.

155
00:07:23,429 --> 00:07:25,222
He's taking so long.

156
00:07:27,016 --> 00:07:27,850
I'll see you.

157
00:07:27,851 --> 00:07:29,810
Yes, I need to go.

158
00:07:47,953 --> 00:07:48,787
Excuse me.

159
00:07:48,788 --> 00:07:51,164
Where is the scholarship application?

160
00:07:51,165 --> 00:07:52,165
Over there.

161
00:07:52,166 --> 00:07:53,501
Thank you.

162
00:08:02,635 --> 00:08:03,636
Kiko!

163
00:08:04,887 --> 00:08:05,679
Kiko.

164
00:08:05,679 --> 00:08:06,347
Jorge?

165
00:08:06,348 --> 00:08:07,722
Don't go.

166
00:08:07,723 --> 00:08:08,599
Huh?

167
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:10,934
Our grandfathers...

168
00:08:10,935 --> 00:08:13,896
They parted and never saw each other again.

169
00:08:15,231 --> 00:08:20,110
We have to right their wrongs in the past.

170
00:08:21,153 --> 00:08:21,862
Jorge.

171
00:08:21,863 --> 00:08:25,406
When I become the
manager of the restaurant,

172
00:08:25,407 --> 00:08:28,952
You can be my assistant manager.
You can...

173
00:08:28,953 --> 00:08:29,995
Jorge!

174
00:08:32,248 --> 00:08:33,791
You're so selfish!

175
00:08:35,459 --> 00:08:37,335
Don’t you get it?

176
00:08:37,336 --> 00:08:40,005
There are a lot of things
I want to do in my life.

177
00:08:41,382 --> 00:08:43,384
I want to study in Manila.

178
00:08:45,135 --> 00:08:48,180
Opportunities like this
are rare for me, Jorge.

179
00:08:49,014 --> 00:08:50,975
Why would I stay here?

180
00:08:53,519 --> 00:08:55,895
Who told you...

181
00:08:55,896 --> 00:08:58,524
that I wanted to be your assistant manager?

182
00:09:00,276 --> 00:09:00,985
I thought...

183
00:09:00,986 --> 00:09:03,362
Our grandparents did the right thing.

184
00:09:04,738 --> 00:09:07,157
We have our own paths in life.

185
00:09:08,242 --> 00:09:10,703
They only chose what was right for them.

186
00:09:11,704 --> 00:09:13,121
No...

187
00:09:13,122 --> 00:09:14,540
Next!

188
00:09:18,127 --> 00:09:19,670
I'm next.

189
00:09:20,879 --> 00:09:22,339
Jorge...

190
00:09:23,007 --> 00:09:25,175
Go home.

191
00:09:26,010 --> 00:09:27,386
Isn't it...

192
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:30,764
Grandpa Tino's funeral today?

193
00:09:34,059 --> 00:09:35,603
You’re next!

194
00:11:03,982 --> 00:11:10,698
SOON TO REOPEN

195
00:11:20,916 --> 00:11:22,375
Let's clean up here.

196
00:11:22,376 --> 00:11:24,043
It's heavy.

197
00:11:24,044 --> 00:11:25,670
I'll help you.

198
00:11:25,671 --> 00:11:27,965
Put it here.

199
00:11:29,967 --> 00:11:31,718
That's good already.

200
00:11:31,719 --> 00:11:33,469
Here, Jorge.

201
00:11:33,470 --> 00:11:35,722
There's a lot to do here.

202
00:11:35,723 --> 00:11:37,224
Yes, actually.

203
00:11:39,935 --> 00:11:40,728
Here, put it here.

204
00:11:40,728 --> 00:11:41,395
No.

205
00:11:41,396 --> 00:11:42,396
Okay, okay.

206
00:11:43,814 --> 00:11:45,773
Okay.

207
00:11:45,774 --> 00:11:48,860
I'll go clean in the kitchen
since there's a lot to fix there.

208
00:11:48,861 --> 00:11:50,696
- Stay here, okay?
- Yes, okay.

209
00:12:04,001 --> 00:12:05,294
Jorge.

210
00:12:06,837 --> 00:12:07,879
How's your guy?

211
00:12:07,880 --> 00:12:09,339
Kiko?

212
00:12:10,883 --> 00:12:12,634
He's okay.

213
00:12:13,886 --> 00:12:18,348
Why didn't he come to
your grandpa's funeral?

214
00:12:20,350 --> 00:12:21,893
He's busy.

215
00:12:21,894 --> 00:12:25,898
He has a lot to do tomorrow.

216
00:12:32,905 --> 00:12:33,906
Jorge?

217
00:12:40,329 --> 00:12:42,080
Forgive me.

218
00:12:44,750 --> 00:12:46,167
Dad.

219
00:12:46,168 --> 00:12:47,920
You're not at fault.

220
00:12:48,712 --> 00:12:50,422
We understand.

221
00:12:54,259 --> 00:12:55,636
Jorge.

222
00:12:57,012 --> 00:12:59,181
I'm sorry.

223
00:13:01,225 --> 00:13:04,602
I wasn't a good father to you.

224
00:13:04,603 --> 00:13:06,605
In any way.

225
00:13:13,237 --> 00:13:15,113
Dad.

226
00:13:16,532 --> 00:13:18,534
Forgive me too.

227
00:13:20,452 --> 00:13:22,621
Jorge.

228
00:13:24,998 --> 00:13:28,543
I couldn’t give you everything.

229
00:13:28,544 --> 00:13:32,004
As much as

230
00:13:32,005 --> 00:13:35,092
what your grandpa gave you.

231
00:13:42,558 --> 00:13:46,727
Aunt Lilia promised

232
00:13:46,728 --> 00:13:50,649
she will manage the restaurant.

233
00:13:52,651 --> 00:13:57,030
She will entrust it to me once I graduate.

234
00:13:58,282 --> 00:14:00,658
Or...

235
00:14:00,659 --> 00:14:04,162
I can manage our new branch.

236
00:14:12,796 --> 00:14:14,798
Son.

237
00:14:16,091 --> 00:14:18,676
I’m running out of time.

238
00:14:18,677 --> 00:14:22,221
I wish I could’ve left
you with some guidance

239
00:14:22,222 --> 00:14:26,226
and opportunities for you to be happy.

240
00:14:28,770 --> 00:14:30,522
Dad.

241
00:14:32,983 --> 00:14:35,861
It's okay.

242
00:14:37,362 --> 00:14:40,198
Thank you.

243
00:14:43,118 --> 00:14:45,495
Thank you, my son.

244
00:15:10,103 --> 00:15:11,854
Will you board the bus?

245
00:15:11,855 --> 00:15:12,856
Bus?

246
00:15:13,774 --> 00:15:15,108
Later.

247
00:15:16,318 --> 00:15:17,319
Okay.

248
00:15:51,645 --> 00:15:55,232
I couldn't let you leave
without saying goodbye.

249
00:15:57,651 --> 00:16:00,112
It's good to see you here, Jorge.

250
00:16:01,321 --> 00:16:04,073
I'm happy for you.

251
00:16:04,074 --> 00:16:05,784
Sincerely.

252
00:16:06,702 --> 00:16:08,245
Thank you.

253
00:16:09,955 --> 00:16:11,957
You do good there.

254
00:16:13,375 --> 00:16:15,167
I'll really do my best.

255
00:16:15,168 --> 00:16:19,631
If not, they'll remove my scholarship.

256
00:16:26,096 --> 00:16:27,596
What's this?

257
00:16:27,597 --> 00:16:30,099
I didn't want to send
this to the post office

258
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:32,686
because it might get lost.

259
00:16:34,062 --> 00:16:36,772
It's why I wanted to
give it straight to you.

260
00:16:36,773 --> 00:16:38,149
You know, Jorge.

261
00:16:38,150 --> 00:16:40,276
We're luckier than our grandparents.

262
00:16:40,277 --> 00:16:41,111
There's Facebook.

263
00:16:41,111 --> 00:16:41,820
Viber.

264
00:16:41,820 --> 00:16:42,446
Twitter.

265
00:16:42,447 --> 00:16:44,030
Instagram.

266
00:16:44,031 --> 00:16:44,865
Line.

267
00:16:44,866 --> 00:16:46,323
There’s a lot.

268
00:16:46,324 --> 00:16:48,994
Do you have accounts for all of those?

269
00:16:49,369 --> 00:16:52,997
It’s impossible not to
update each other, Jorge.

270
00:16:52,998 --> 00:16:54,707
Of course.

271
00:16:54,708 --> 00:16:57,377
You'll know immediately when I marry.

272
00:17:00,005 --> 00:17:01,131
Sorry.

273
00:17:01,631 --> 00:17:02,758
Bad joke.

274
00:17:05,343 --> 00:17:07,262
Bad joke.

275
00:17:09,431 --> 00:17:11,475
Will you board the bus or not?

276
00:17:12,893 --> 00:17:14,686
Only him.

277
00:17:17,355 --> 00:17:19,191
Only him.

278
00:17:30,952 --> 00:17:32,078
I have to go, Jorge.

279
00:17:32,079 --> 00:17:33,162
Yes.

280
00:17:33,163 --> 00:17:34,706
Go.

281
00:18:33,014 --> 00:18:35,683
For my dear Kiko,

282
00:18:35,684 --> 00:18:40,104
You didn't get a chance to read
Grandpa Bong's letter to Grandpa Tino.

283
00:18:40,105 --> 00:18:43,650
But I did.

284
00:18:44,276 --> 00:18:47,904
It's too sad for me to repeat it.

285
00:18:48,613 --> 00:18:50,865
I realized it's hard to wait

286
00:18:50,866 --> 00:18:54,286
when you don't know if there's
still something you're waiting for.

287
00:18:59,374 --> 00:19:01,877
So, I thought...

288
00:19:03,336 --> 00:19:05,505
I won't wait for you anymore.

289
00:19:07,090 --> 00:19:10,677
I won't wait many years for you.

290
00:19:11,261 --> 00:19:13,471
That’s why...

291
00:19:13,472 --> 00:19:16,183
I will follow you to Manila.

292
00:19:17,893 --> 00:19:21,687
I will study as well.

293
00:19:21,688 --> 00:19:23,814
I will follow you.

294
00:19:23,815 --> 00:19:25,858
So we could be together.

295
00:19:25,859 --> 00:19:28,195
Wait!

296
00:21:41,286 --> 00:21:43,412
Where's the lighter, Lilia?

297
00:21:43,413 --> 00:21:47,124
Here. Continue preparing there.

298
00:21:47,125 --> 00:21:48,125
Ruth!

299
00:21:48,126 --> 00:21:49,418
Yes, Auntie?

300
00:21:49,419 --> 00:21:50,836
Make sure...

301
00:21:50,837 --> 00:21:53,380
They will taste Jorge’s miki.

302
00:21:53,381 --> 00:21:55,424
So we could put it into the menu.

303
00:21:55,425 --> 00:21:57,092
Of course, Auntie.

304
00:21:57,093 --> 00:21:58,886
Jorge would love that.

305
00:21:58,887 --> 00:22:00,722
Lilia.

306
00:22:01,264 --> 00:22:02,848
I wrote everyone.

307
00:22:02,849 --> 00:22:05,559
But I have a problem.
Her name is Socorro.

308
00:22:05,560 --> 00:22:07,436
Does it have one "r" or two?

309
00:22:07,437 --> 00:22:08,980
Two R’s.

310
00:22:25,538 --> 00:22:27,247
They're here!

311
00:22:27,248 --> 00:22:28,332
How was the travel?

312
00:22:28,333 --> 00:22:30,793
- How are you?
- I’m good.

313
00:22:30,794 --> 00:22:32,711
Here, let me help you.

314
00:22:32,712 --> 00:22:34,756
Come inside.

315
00:22:43,056 --> 00:22:46,851
What are you doing?

316
00:22:47,644 --> 00:22:49,728
How are the people from Manila?

317
00:22:49,729 --> 00:22:51,522
We're okay, Auntie.

318
00:22:51,523 --> 00:22:52,523
Is it your semester break?

319
00:22:52,524 --> 00:22:54,441
Yes. It's our semester break.

320
00:22:54,442 --> 00:22:57,653
You arrived at the right time.

321
00:22:57,654 --> 00:23:00,697
- You're so pretty, Auntie.
- The prayer will start soon.

322
00:23:00,698 --> 00:23:02,908
Of course.

323
00:23:02,909 --> 00:23:04,410
Did you eat already?

324
00:23:04,411 --> 00:23:06,870
Not yet. I'm really hungry.

325
00:23:06,871 --> 00:23:08,664
We'll go cook then.

326
00:23:08,665 --> 00:23:11,500
We'll prepare the food.

327
00:23:11,501 --> 00:23:12,127
Okay, Auntie.

328
00:23:12,128 --> 00:23:13,378
Okay!

329
00:23:24,848 --> 00:23:26,182
Jorge.

330
00:23:28,143 --> 00:23:29,144
Kiko.

331
00:23:31,938 --> 00:23:34,232
I prepared your room.

332
00:24:29,496 --> 00:24:31,539
I'm so tired.

333
00:24:44,469 --> 00:24:46,095
Jorge.

334
00:24:56,981 --> 00:24:58,942
What?

335
00:25:49,158 --> 00:25:50,326
Dad.

336
00:25:50,910 --> 00:25:51,661
What?

337
00:25:51,662 --> 00:25:52,954
Can I see that?

338
00:25:57,208 --> 00:25:58,751
May I borrow your pen?

339
00:26:11,889 --> 00:26:14,267
Who's Primitivo?

340
00:26:15,810 --> 00:26:18,021
Grandpa Tino's friend.

341
00:26:26,237 --> 00:26:28,156
What are you praying for?

342
00:26:31,200 --> 00:26:35,370
Can't I pray in silence
so it will come true?

343
00:26:35,371 --> 00:26:38,332
Jorge, you're not blowing
out candles on a cake.

344
00:26:38,333 --> 00:26:42,252
The dead are listening
so they can help us get what we want.

345
00:26:42,253 --> 00:26:45,965
I'm just saying, you can tell me.

346
00:26:47,300 --> 00:26:50,093
Do I really have to tell you?

347
00:26:50,094 --> 00:26:51,219
Yes.

348
00:26:51,220 --> 00:26:53,681
Unless you already got what you wanted.

349
00:26:56,726 --> 00:26:58,101
Get inside.

350
00:26:58,102 --> 00:27:01,230
The prayer will start.

351
00:27:22,210 --> 00:27:24,670
In the name of the Father,
the Son, the Holy Spirit.

352
00:27:24,671 --> 00:27:25,421
Amen.

353
00:27:25,422 --> 00:27:30,134
I believe in God, the Father Almighty...

354
00:27:49,153 --> 00:27:53,950
Our Father who art in Heaven...

355
00:27:56,911 --> 00:28:02,708
Blessed are the souls of
those who enter your Kingdom.

356
00:28:02,709 --> 00:28:06,628
Eternal rest grant unto the soul

357
00:28:06,629 --> 00:28:08,547
for the soul of Socorro,

358
00:28:08,548 --> 00:28:10,424
for the soul of Teresa,

359
00:28:10,425 --> 00:28:15,304
for the soul of Primitivo,
for the soul of Celestino...

360
00:28:25,500 --> 00:28:30,000
"All the Things I Leave You"
